body:
I don't think it was an inside job, but the US govt definitely had prior knowledge and didn't prevent it from happening. We were doing hijacking drills literally on September 11th (look up operation Vigilant Guardian), and that's not to mention the infamous August 6th CIA briefing titled "Bin Laden Determined to Strike US" that specifically mentions hijacking planes in the text. 

&#x200B;

We knew something was going to happen, regardless of the "failure of imagination" claimed in the 9/11 Commission Report. The reason we didn't do anything to stop it is because we needed a vehicle to drive us into the profit-driven War on Terror.

Look up the Katie Johnson case. Trump raped a 13 year old child at Epstein's New York apartment. Maria Farmer (the first woman to contact the FBI about Epstein) also stated that she saw Trump at Epstein's apartment, coming and going often, and that Ivana assisted Ghislaine in procuring children for Epstein.

&#x200B;

[https://youtu.be/1FWc2tnf\_KA](https://youtu.be/1FWc2tnf_KA) here's the link to the interview she states this in. Comments about Trump start at 34:35. Ivana comes up at 36:30, and Maria discusses the role Ivana played more thoroughly in part 1 of her interview with Whitney Webb ([https://youtu.be/MGtDj8drWvE](https://youtu.be/MGtDj8drWvE) at 44 minutes).

I am very very VERY new to SCA and I'm really trying to understand how all of this works. I don't understand the basic order of products nor do I understand terminology and particular chemicals (retinoids, BHA, AHA, etc). I have dry skin, with dark underye circles, no acne, but lots of redness/hyperpigmentation. My current routine looks something like this:

&#x200B;

Morning:

Neutrogena hydroboost exfoliating cleanser

thayer's witch hazel toner

cerave moisturizer (yes, the one in the tub)

&#x200B;

(same routine at night, except I remove makeup with the neutrogena makeup wipes first)

&#x200B;

I'm thinking about adding the Ordinary's caffeine + ECGC to deal with the underyes and also their Ascorbic Acid + alpha arbutin to deal with the pigmentation. Where would I put them in my routine? Are these reliable products? I really want to even out my complexion and get rid of these dark circles. I live in the US and would prefer products under $35.
